Now, wheelbarrow!

42
00:03:14,880 --> 00:03:28,880
This phone's crap and the network's lagging.

43
00:03:29,120 --> 00:03:30,540
Plus the update ruined my fighter.

44
00:03:31,580 --> 00:03:32,680
Likely excuses.

45
00:03:33,080 --> 00:03:34,320
Face it, you've got no game.

46
00:03:34,960 --> 00:03:35,760
Next player's up.

47
00:03:37,520 --> 00:03:38,620
It's all yours.

48
00:03:38,900 --> 00:03:39,380
Good luck.

49
00:03:39,780 --> 00:03:41,720
Don't lose, or we have to help her.

50
00:03:42,940 --> 00:03:44,520
This will be child's play.

51
00:03:44,880 --> 00:03:45,880
Hmm.

52
00:03:49,880 --> 00:03:50,360
Ah!

53
00:03:51,240 --> 00:03:55,380
The hell!

54
00:03:55,700 --> 00:03:56,980
You didn't even touch her!

55
00:03:57,400 --> 00:03:59,680
At least I got in a few good punches!

56
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:02,160
Sorry, you're both losers.

57
00:04:04,380 --> 00:04:05,400
I don't hit girls.

58
00:04:07,340 --> 00:04:10,560
I won the bet, but it doesn't feel like a win.

59
00:04:10,860 --> 00:04:12,780
Try not to screw up this next mission, okay?

60
00:04:13,820 --> 00:04:14,740
Start talking.

61
00:04:15,140 --> 00:04:15,680
What's up?

62
00:04:16,360 --> 00:04:17,680
You've piqued my interest.

63
00:04:19,880 --> 00:04:22,660
Our client's in love with a woman from a martial arts family.

64
00:04:23,300 --> 00:04:25,100
He's confessed his love repeatedly.

65
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:28,420
Problem is, her dad's a hand-to-hand master.

66
00:04:28,960 --> 00:04:31,500
He'll only approve a marriage if the groom confessed him.

67
00:04:31,500 --> 00:04:34,640
They've also never accepted a non-fighter into the family.

68
00:04:34,640 --> 00:04:34,680
They've also never accepted a non-fighter into the family.

69
00:04:34,680 --> 00:04:42,520
We've also captured a non-fighter into the family.

70
00:04:42,680 --> 00:04:48,520
What about a tribe?

71
00:04:50,860 --> 00:04:54,540
Our guys fought over and over again.

72
00:04:54,540 --> 00:04:57,040
and failed each time.

73
00:04:58,360 --> 00:05:01,320
That's because Big Bad Dad has unique skills,

74
00:05:01,720 --> 00:05:02,980
some secret technique.

75
00:05:03,700 --> 00:05:05,800
The client has no idea how to beat us.

76
00:05:09,540 --> 00:05:12,720
Analyze the father's moves so our client can win and get married.

77
00:05:13,720 --> 00:05:16,500
Hey, can't you just look at a pic and figure them out?

78
00:05:18,120 --> 00:05:20,600
Hmm. I doubt it.

79
00:05:20,600 --> 00:05:25,180
Here. This photo was taken before one of the fights.

80
00:05:29,220 --> 00:05:30,700
Huh. That's sad.

81
00:05:30,880 --> 00:05:32,840
They definitely look like they're in love with each other.

82
00:05:34,180 --> 00:05:35,720
Solve this. And quickly.

83
00:05:36,720 --> 00:05:38,100
He's running out of time.

84
00:05:46,460 --> 00:05:49,280
Come on, man. Stare at the picture and see how the Master fights.

85
00:05:49,280 --> 00:05:51,820
That would save us like so much work.

86
00:05:52,300 --> 00:05:53,340
His skills are secret.

87
00:05:53,940 --> 00:05:57,100
I need you to visit the scene and act as my eyes.

88
00:05:57,980 --> 00:05:59,360
Fine. I'll go.

89
00:05:59,760 --> 00:06:00,360
We lost.

90
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:01,060
Fair and square.

91
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:07,640
You ready?

92
00:06:16,600 --> 00:06:17,240
Dive.

93
00:06:17,240 --> 00:06:25,840
An engagement pick before my big win.

94
00:06:26,720 --> 00:06:27,500
Very funny.

95
00:06:28,020 --> 00:06:29,260
My dad is so stubborn.

96
00:06:29,560 --> 00:06:31,040
He's never gonna go easy on you.

97
00:06:31,240 --> 00:06:32,320
I trained hard this year.

98
00:06:32,800 --> 00:06:34,460
Now I've got my own secret skills.

99
00:06:34,740 --> 00:06:35,260
Just wait.

100
00:06:35,420 --> 00:06:36,280
You'll see him soon.

101
00:06:36,800 --> 00:06:38,960
You think you're gonna win every time you fight.

102
00:06:39,480 --> 00:06:40,780
How's that working out for you?

103
00:06:40,780 --> 00:06:40,860
Yeah.

104
00:06:40,860 --> 00:06:45,500
Remember the first time you paid a visit?

105
00:06:45,500 --> 00:07:11,380
We'll see you soon.

106
00:07:11,380 --> 00:07:13,100
We'll see you soon.

107
00:07:13,100 --> 00:07:18,600
We've not accepted an outsider in many generations.

108
00:07:19,200 --> 00:07:20,340
Your efforts are wasted.

109
00:07:20,760 --> 00:07:21,700
Leave this mountain.

110
00:07:21,700 --> 00:07:23,500
What do people say?

111
00:07:29,500 --> 00:07:30,720
Oh, no!

112
00:07:31,140 --> 00:07:33,620
I've come to marry you!

113
00:07:36,640 --> 00:07:38,580
What are you laughing for?

114
00:07:38,680 --> 00:07:39,580
Aren't you embarrassed?

115
00:07:43,100 --> 00:07:49,580
Help him.

116
00:07:49,580 --> 00:07:50,860
Take him into the house.

117
00:07:55,320 --> 00:07:57,040
Stop that, you idiot.

118
00:07:57,460 --> 00:07:59,220
Oh, man, that was hilarious.

119
00:07:59,960 --> 00:08:00,860
I bit it so hard.

120
00:08:00,860 --> 00:08:02,260
Don't shout this time, all right?

121
00:08:03,920 --> 00:08:05,080
But I want to.

122
00:08:05,100 --> 00:08:05,820
Absolutely not!

123
00:08:05,840 --> 00:08:07,740
Maybe you're forgetting what you told me first.

124
00:08:08,020 --> 00:08:09,120
I've still got the evidence.

125
00:08:09,720 --> 00:08:11,400
Why don't you throw that antique in the trash?

126
00:08:11,540 --> 00:08:12,620
Here, give it to me!

127
00:08:13,100 --> 00:08:18,860
Look at you blushing.

128
00:08:19,140 --> 00:08:19,880
It's so cute.

129
00:08:20,480 --> 00:08:21,060
Moron!

130
00:08:21,480 --> 00:08:22,800
Stop adding your own lines.

131
00:08:23,580 --> 00:08:27,900
Suen, there's something that I have to tell you.

132
00:08:28,940 --> 00:08:32,120
Dad's student asked for my hand in marriage.

133
00:08:32,120 --> 00:08:39,580
And did your father say yes?

134
00:08:40,580 --> 00:08:41,440
Who cares?

135
00:08:42,080 --> 00:08:42,940
I didn't.

136
00:08:43,460 --> 00:08:45,500
It's my hand to give and no one else's.

137
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:47,780
Either way, we both have a mountain to climb.

138
00:08:48,700 --> 00:08:49,920
Don't be late, okay?

139
00:08:49,920 --> 00:08:56,740
Now I get it.

140
00:08:57,740 --> 00:08:59,240
He's running out of time.

141
00:08:59,400 --> 00:08:59,880
Be quick.

142
00:09:01,300 --> 00:09:02,420
Stay smart.

143
00:09:02,800 --> 00:09:04,440
You understand how this power works.

144
00:09:04,440 --> 00:09:06,000
The same photo can't be used twice.

145
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:07,100
The same photo can't be used twice.

146
00:09:07,760 --> 00:09:09,760
This is our only chance.

147
00:09:09,760 --> 00:09:19,720
I have to climb up the mountain on foot?

148
00:09:19,720 --> 00:09:22,340
The chill link picked us to torture me!

149
00:09:31,600 --> 00:09:33,160
You're walking too slow.

150
00:09:33,380 --> 00:09:34,680
It's two hours to their home.

151
00:09:34,680 --> 00:09:39,280
Don't kick a man while he's down.

152
00:09:39,620 --> 00:09:41,520
Why am I always the one who suffers?

153
00:09:56,320 --> 00:09:56,960
Hello?

154
00:09:57,820 --> 00:09:59,120
Hey, Lou, are you listening?

155
00:09:59,120 --> 00:10:05,520
Are you there yet?

156
00:10:05,720 --> 00:10:06,740
Almost at the top.

157
00:10:07,480 --> 00:10:08,020
Run next.

158
00:10:08,140 --> 00:10:08,360
Wait.

159
00:10:09,020 --> 00:10:09,840
You're early.

160
00:10:10,460 --> 00:10:10,840
Hang tight.

161
00:10:12,900 --> 00:10:15,920
What futile trick does he hope to use against me this time?

162
00:10:17,240 --> 00:10:18,160
Now you're good.

163
00:10:20,140 --> 00:10:21,820
Shout like your life depends on it.

164
00:10:23,260 --> 00:10:23,740
Uyung!

165
00:10:23,980 --> 00:10:25,840
I've come to marry you!

166
00:10:26,120 --> 00:10:27,700
It's the same every year.

167
00:10:27,700 --> 00:10:29,680
Can't you think of something more creative?

168
00:10:36,860 --> 00:10:39,000
This time I'm going to defeat you.

169
00:10:41,420 --> 00:10:43,700
Firstly, you weren't raised in martial arts,

170
00:10:43,840 --> 00:10:45,560
and amateurs aren't welcome in my home.

171
00:10:45,860 --> 00:10:47,660
Secondly, you're younger than my daughter.

172
00:10:47,800 --> 00:10:49,580
I'll never accept this pairing.

173
00:10:49,900 --> 00:10:51,560
Left palm out, right hand back.

174
00:10:51,900 --> 00:10:52,440
Stand tall.

175
00:10:54,100 --> 00:10:55,540
Can you not follow directions?

176
00:10:55,840 --> 00:10:56,380
Reverse it!

177
00:10:56,380 --> 00:10:59,020
Can't even hold a simple stance.

178
00:10:59,180 --> 00:10:59,980
You're hopeless!

179
00:11:00,160 --> 00:11:01,580
Quick, deflect with your left hand.

180
00:11:03,220 --> 00:11:04,940
Have you never been in a fight before?

181
00:11:05,180 --> 00:11:06,440
Why are you moving so slow?

182
00:11:07,400 --> 00:11:09,040
Don't sit there, on your feet!

183
00:11:12,300 --> 00:11:13,600
Careful, he's going high.

184
00:11:13,800 --> 00:11:14,000
Duck!

185
00:11:15,320 --> 00:11:16,040
Plant your right foot.

186
00:11:16,640 --> 00:11:17,320
Limit his movements.

187
00:11:17,840 --> 00:11:18,540
Center yourself!

188
00:11:18,540 --> 00:11:23,060
Shut up!

189
00:11:23,280 --> 00:11:24,640
You're giving me a headache!

190
00:11:25,280 --> 00:11:27,240
Please, you need my help to do this.

191
00:11:27,480 --> 00:11:28,040
As if.

192
00:11:28,220 --> 00:11:29,300
Just sit back and watch.

193
00:11:29,540 --> 00:11:31,060
I'll show you what I'm capable of.

194
00:11:31,220 --> 00:11:33,100
Your movement's like basic economy.

195
00:11:33,280 --> 00:11:35,440
It's obvious that your training is subpar.

196
00:11:35,840 --> 00:11:38,700
Old man, you'll take that back when I've beaten you.

197
00:11:38,800 --> 00:11:39,340
Shall we?

198
00:11:39,340 --> 00:11:41,980
You're disrespectful, little brat!

199
00:11:41,980 --> 00:11:52,940
What's this technique he's using?

200
00:11:53,120 --> 00:11:54,920
He's predicting your father's attacks.

201
00:11:58,200 --> 00:11:59,580
Don't go overboard.

202
00:11:59,920 --> 00:12:01,000
Take a few hits, too.

203
00:12:03,440 --> 00:12:04,860
You taught me?

204
00:12:04,980 --> 00:12:05,840
Special move?

205
00:12:06,220 --> 00:12:07,500
Snatch the club!

206
00:12:07,500 --> 00:12:19,080
What just happened?

207
00:12:19,860 --> 00:12:21,940
Was that the secret move?

208
00:12:22,520 --> 00:12:24,140
The one our client could never beat?

209
00:12:31,140 --> 00:12:33,820
Again, I need a better view.

210
00:12:37,500 --> 00:12:40,720
I've been trying to learn this move for the past decade.

211
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:42,720
I love her.

212
00:12:43,180 --> 00:12:44,780
Please, Master, approve our marriage.

213
00:12:46,080 --> 00:12:48,520
So, you've finally gathered the courage.

214
00:12:48,800 --> 00:12:50,520
You must know what you ask.

215
00:12:52,880 --> 00:12:54,640
Show me you deserve her hand.

216
00:12:54,640 --> 00:13:15,440
It's no use.

217
00:13:15,440 --> 00:13:17,720
I can't figure out that punch.

218
00:13:18,520 --> 00:13:19,900
And everything hurts.

219
00:13:20,860 --> 00:13:22,980
I think I might pass out.

220
00:13:24,740 --> 00:13:26,060
Hands have gotten numb.

221
00:13:27,060 --> 00:13:28,920
This must be the end.

222
00:13:29,600 --> 00:13:30,600
It's not over yet.

223
00:13:31,240 --> 00:13:31,860
You're kidding.

224
00:13:32,440 --> 00:13:34,180
I can barely move this body.

225
00:13:34,840 --> 00:13:36,160
No way does he keep fighting.

226
00:13:37,020 --> 00:13:38,220
He gets up.

227
00:13:38,700 --> 00:13:40,280
I saw it with my own eyes.

228
00:13:40,280 --> 00:13:44,000
I'm seriously at my limit.

229
00:13:44,860 --> 00:13:47,320
How did he find the strength to stand up again?

230
00:13:47,320 --> 00:13:47,380
I'm seriously at my limit.

231
00:14:10,280 --> 00:14:13,540
Please, call the fight off.

232
00:14:14,280 --> 00:14:16,120
I just won't marry anyone, ever.

233
00:14:16,120 --> 00:14:16,240
I just won't marry anyone, ever.

234
00:14:16,240 --> 00:14:46,220
I just won't marry anyone, ever.

235
00:14:46,240 --> 00:14:50,100
How's it going?

236
00:14:50,360 --> 00:14:51,940
You guys figure out the Master's trick?

237
00:14:55,940 --> 00:14:58,000
So, that bad, huh?

238
00:14:58,840 --> 00:15:00,380
A little complicated for you guys?

239
00:15:00,720 --> 00:15:01,600
He's too fast.

240
00:15:02,080 --> 00:15:02,860
No way to see it.

241
00:15:03,600 --> 00:15:04,200
We failed.

242
00:15:06,460 --> 00:15:06,940
Gotcha.

243
00:15:07,320 --> 00:15:07,900
No biggie.

244
00:15:08,580 --> 00:15:09,920
I didn't know it'd be so hard.

245
00:15:11,240 --> 00:15:13,860
Well, at least you tried your best for him.

246
00:15:13,860 --> 00:15:19,360
By the way, how'd you find out about this whole thing?

247
00:15:20,360 --> 00:15:21,680
That part doesn't matter.

248
00:15:21,780 --> 00:15:23,560
Last month, I was passing by a dojo.

249
00:15:24,860 --> 00:15:29,160
There have been lots of stories about murders lately, and I was kinda creeped out.

250
00:15:29,520 --> 00:15:32,000
So I thought maybe I should learn to fight.

251
00:15:32,320 --> 00:15:35,500
That's when I met Suwen, the owner of the dojo.

252
00:15:35,500 --> 00:15:38,260
Hello, miss.

253
00:15:38,680 --> 00:15:39,520
Looking to learn?

254
00:15:40,320 --> 00:15:40,500
Huh?

255
00:15:51,300 --> 00:15:53,240
Come in and have a seat if you're interested.

256
00:15:53,780 --> 00:15:55,940
Or if you simply want to chat, I'm all ears.

257
00:15:55,940 --> 00:16:00,340
Year after year, he's fought the father of the woman he loves.

258
00:16:01,060 --> 00:16:03,160
But he always fails.

259
00:16:03,160 --> 00:16:13,380
The dad wanted someone from a martial arts family as a son-in-law.

260
00:16:14,280 --> 00:16:17,840
That's why this client trained so hard and opened his own dojo.

261
00:16:19,760 --> 00:16:23,800
Everyone laughed at him and her family, saying they were all stubborn.

262
00:16:24,700 --> 00:16:26,860
That things like this didn't matter nowadays.

263
00:16:26,860 --> 00:16:41,160
Go back inside.

264
00:16:41,760 --> 00:16:43,900
We've seen the last of your failed suitor.

265
00:16:46,220 --> 00:16:48,340
That poor fool.

266
00:16:48,540 --> 00:16:50,180
He never should have challenged me.

267
00:16:50,980 --> 00:16:53,860
And the one who should have proved himself...

268
00:16:53,860 --> 00:17:01,000
Master, please stop.

269
00:17:02,100 --> 00:17:03,100
I surrender.

270
00:17:03,820 --> 00:17:04,640
I can't.

271
00:17:05,020 --> 00:17:07,680
Gave up a long time ago.

272
00:17:18,440 --> 00:17:19,780
Hey, uh...

273
00:17:19,780 --> 00:17:21,680
Isn't this against your sacred rules?

274
00:17:22,780 --> 00:17:23,720
Don't worry.

275
00:17:23,860 --> 00:17:25,440
I'll keep us in line.

276
00:17:33,240 --> 00:17:34,240
Oh, Jan!

277
00:17:34,600 --> 00:17:36,440
I've come to bury you!

278
00:17:37,920 --> 00:17:40,180
I've devoted myself to this.

279
00:17:40,740 --> 00:17:43,160
Living each day by a disciplined diet.

280
00:17:43,860 --> 00:17:45,540
Sacrificing my time and body.

281
00:17:46,140 --> 00:17:47,500
Training like a madman.

282
00:17:48,180 --> 00:17:51,200
But I never realized how strong her father was.

283
00:17:51,700 --> 00:17:52,860
I can't defeat him.

284
00:17:53,280 --> 00:17:54,660
Nor will I outlive him.

285
00:17:55,560 --> 00:17:59,360
And as he has passed, the stairs got harder to climb.

286
00:17:59,620 --> 00:18:00,220
Hold on.

287
00:18:00,680 --> 00:18:02,140
You two have been in love forever.

288
00:18:02,880 --> 00:18:04,380
Why do you even need his approval?

289
00:18:05,380 --> 00:18:06,980
I still persevere.

290
00:18:06,980 --> 00:18:10,820
Because I promised my Ooyang a proper marriage.

291
00:18:11,240 --> 00:18:12,860
I refuse to let her down.

292
00:18:16,360 --> 00:18:19,700
I have a plan.

293
00:18:20,240 --> 00:18:21,160
You want to hear it?

294
00:18:21,160 --> 00:18:31,320
Su-Wen.

295
00:18:31,420 --> 00:18:32,220
Su-Wen.

296
00:18:32,220 --> 00:18:46,340
Next year, can we fight at the bottom?

297
00:18:50,340 --> 00:18:52,180
My blessing.

298
00:19:02,220 --> 00:19:10,300
Why didn't you let go sooner?

299
00:19:12,760 --> 00:19:16,200
Even my grandchild is a reputable fighter now.

300
00:19:16,920 --> 00:19:19,240
And yet this man couldn't defeat me.

301
00:19:19,800 --> 00:19:23,300
How was I supposed to approve of him, to accept his weakness?

302
00:19:24,320 --> 00:19:27,640
So, what's the hardest thing about love?

303
00:19:28,180 --> 00:19:31,920
People have asked that question for a long, long time.

304
00:19:32,880 --> 00:19:33,460
And now?

305
00:19:34,020 --> 00:19:35,960
Why don't you throw that antique in the trash?

306
00:19:36,120 --> 00:19:37,200
Here, give it to me!

307
00:19:37,520 --> 00:19:40,360
I think I finally know the answer.

308
00:19:40,360 --> 00:19:43,360
I don't know what to do.

309
00:19:43,360 --> 00:19:46,120
What should I do?

310
00:19:46,960 --> 00:19:51,200
Is everything going to happen now?

311
00:19:52,200 --> 00:19:55,200
I'm so sad to see you in the past.

312
00:19:55,740 --> 00:19:59,080
I don't know why the answer has left too much.

313
00:19:59,080 --> 00:20:03,820
猜疑着的人都谢谢出现过

314
00:20:33,820 --> 00:21:03,800
Thank you.

315
00:21:03,820 --> 00:21:33,800
Thank you.

